<title>USA: U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA rice export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Sales of 96,300 MT were nearly three times the prior week's level and 38 percent above the 4-week average.  Japan (50,100 MT) was the dominant purchaser, followed by Turkey (16,300 MT--all rough), Costa Rica (15,000 MT--all rough), and the Leeward and Windward Islands (7,000 MT).</p>
<p>Exports of 47,400 MT were up 14 percent from the prior week, but down 16 percent from the 4-week average.  The primary destinations were Japan (20,200 MT), Jamaica (8,400 MT), Saudi Arabia (4,900 MT), the Netherlands (3,900 MT), and Canada (2,900 MT).</p>
</text>
